---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { brand } from '../config/brand';

const lastUpdated = '10 September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy & copyright"
  description={`Privacy policy and copyright terms for ${brand.name}: personal data, reuse of guides, and brand assets.`}
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <section class="py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <p class="text-topper font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-heading text-h1 font-semibold text-text">Privacy &amp; copyright</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      <p class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm font-semibold">
        <a href="#privacy" class="text-primary hover:text-primary-light">Privacy</a>
        <a href="#copyright" class="text-primary hover:text-primary-light">Copyright &amp; reuse</a>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lead leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
        This page covers how {brand.name} (“we”) handles personal data and how our content may be used.
        It is written for transparency under the EU GDPR and Italian copyright law (L. 633/1941). It is not
        legal advice.
      </p>

      <div class="prose-privacy mt-10 space-y-8 text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        <section id="privacy">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-h3 font-semibold text-text">1. Controller</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The data controller is {brand.name}, operating the website at{' '}
            <a href={brand.url} class="font-semibold text-primary hover:text-primary-light">{brand.url}</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            For privacy requests (access, erasure, questions), use the{' '}
            <a href="/contact" class="font-semibold text-primary hover:text-primary-light">contact form</a>
            {' '}and mention “privacy” in your message. We do not publish a public inbox address, to reduce spam.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-h3 font-semibold text-text">2. What we process and why</h2>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-text">Contact form:</strong> name, email, and message, so we can reply.
              Legal basis: steps at your request before a contract / legitimate interest in answering
              inquiries (GDPR Art. 6(1)(b) or (f)).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-text">Community join (Tally):</strong> answers you submit in the join
              form (and any redirect you choose, such as WhatsApp). Legal basis: your request to join
              (Art. 6(1)(b)) and/or consent where the form asks for it (Art. 6(1)(a)).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-text">Hosting logs:</strong> standard technical logs from our static
              host (GitHub Pages) may include IP address and user agent for security and delivery.
              Legal basis: legitimate interest in running a secure website (Art. 6(1)(f)).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-text">Theme preference:</strong> dark/light mode stored in your
              browser (<code class="text-sm text-text">localStorage</code>) so the site remembers your choice.
              This is a technical preference for the service you requested.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We do <strong class="text-text">not</strong> run site analytics (for example Google Analytics)
            and we do not sell personal data.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-h3 font-semibold text-text">3. Processors and recipients</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">We use these providers to deliver features you request:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-text">Formspree</strong> — contact form delivery
              (<a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/" class="ml-1 text-primary hover:text-primary-light" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">(privacy)</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-text">Tally</strong> — community join form
              <a href="https://tally.so/help/privacy-policy" class="ml-1 text-primary hover:text-primary-light" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">(privacy)</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-text">GitHub Pages</strong> — website hosting
              <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" class="ml-1 text-primary hover:text-primary-light" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">(privacy)</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Some providers may process data outside the European Economic Area. Where that happens,
            they rely on mechanisms such as Standard Contractual Clauses or other safeguards described
            in their policies. Details are in each provider’s privacy notice.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-h3 font-semibold text-text">4. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Under Italian rules (Garante Privacy cookie guidelines and Art. 122 of the Privacy Code),
            <strong class="text-text">technical</strong> cookies and similar tools that are strictly
            necessary for a service you request do not need a consent banner. Non-technical tracking
            needs prior consent.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">On first visit we aim to use only what is needed to show the site:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
            <li>Theme preference in local storage (technical).</li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-text">Optional embeds banner:</strong> once per browser we ask whether
              to allow Luma calendar, Google Maps, Instagram, and TikTok embeds. Your choice is stored in
              local storage (<code class="text-sm text-text">milanpost_optional_embeds</code>).
              <strong class="text-text">Accept</strong> loads those embeds automatically on later visits.
              <strong class="text-text">Not now</strong> (or ×) keeps them off until you load one
              manually (per widget or “Load Instagram &amp; TikTok”) or change settings via footer
              <em>Embed settings</em>.
            </li>
            <li>No social embed scripts run on first paint before that choice or an explicit Load click.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Map pages that use OpenStreetMap tiles request map imagery so the map you opened can
            display. See
            <a href="https://wiki.osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy" class="text-primary hover:text-primary-light" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OSM Foundation privacy</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-h3 font-semibold text-text">5. Retention</h2>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
            <li>Contact messages: kept as long as needed to handle your request, then deleted or archived only if we must for legal reasons.</li>
            <li>Tally responses: according to our Tally workspace settings and the purpose of the join process.</li>
            <li>Hosting logs: according to the host’s retention practices.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-h3 font-semibold text-text">6. Your rights</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You may request access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, and objection
            where applicable under GDPR, and withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.
            Use the <a href="/contact" class="font-semibold text-primary hover:text-primary-light">contact form</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You may lodge a complaint with the Italian Data Protection Authority
            (<a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it" class="font-semibold text-primary hover:text-primary-light" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Garante per la protezione dei dati personali</a>)
            or another EU supervisory authority where you live or work.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-h3 font-semibold text-text">7. Children</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The site is aimed at adults arranging life and community in Milan. We do not knowingly
            collect data from children for marketing.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-h3 font-semibold text-text">8. Changes</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We may update this page when our tools or practices change. The “Last updated” date at the
            top will change when we do.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="copyright" class="border-t border-border pt-10">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-h3 font-semibold text-text">9. Copyright and reuse</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Unless a page says otherwise, all original content on this website — including guides, articles,
            glossaries, copy, graphics, and brand artwork — is protected by copyright. © {new Date().getFullYear()}{' '}
            {brand.name}. <strong class="text-text">All rights reserved.</strong>
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">You may:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
            <li>Read and share links to our pages.</li>
            <li>Quote short excerpts with clear attribution and a link back to the original page.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">You may <strong class="text-text">not</strong>, without prior written permission:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
            <li>Copy, republish, or mirror substantial parts of our guides or pages.</li>
            <li>Scrape the site to build a competing dataset, feed, or product.</li>
            <li>Use our name, logo, or branding in a way that suggests endorsement or affiliation.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Official maps, open data, and third-party embeds remain owned by their respective rights holders
            and are subject to their licences. Permission requests:{' '}
            <a href="/contact" class="font-semibold text-primary hover:text-primary-light">contact form</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
